    "title": "Why beginners think they know EVERYTHING \ud83e\udd2f",
    "category": "general",
    "hook_type": "why_hook",
    "video_path": "/Users/geniusbeats/MoneyPrinterTurbo/Videos/2026-09-15_100836_the-dunning-kruger-effect-why-the-least-skilled-people-are-t_76af4bfe/the-dunning-kruger-effect-why-the-least-skilled-people-are-t-1.mp4",
    "description": "Have you ever noticed that the least skilled person in the room is often the most confident? That is the Dunning-Kruger effect in action! When you first start learning something, you lack the knowledge to realize how much you do not know, leading to an irrational peak in confidence. Real expertise only comes after you realize how much learning lies ahead. Have you ever caught yourself falling for this illusion? Drop a comment below!\n\n\ud83d\udd17 More facts + early access: tinyurl.com/238zsuaa\n\n#DunningKruger #PsychologyFacts #SelfImprovement #MindsetShift #LearnOnTikTok"
  },
