    "title": "The REAL reason nostalgia feels so good... \ud83e\udde0\u2728",
    "category": "general",
    "hook_type": "curiosity_hook",
    "video_path": "/Users/geniusbeats/MoneyPrinterTurbo/Videos/2026-09-15_100958_why-nostalgia-feels-so-good-the-psychology-of-missing-the-pa_c073ea19/why-nostalgia-feels-so-good-the-psychology-of-missing-the-pa-1.mp4",
    "description": "Have you ever wondered why listening to a song from your childhood or playing an old video game instantly puts a smile on your face? It turns out nostalgia isn't just a random memory\u2014it's your brain's secret survival tool! When stress or uncertainty hits, your mind rewinds to past moments of comfort and security. This simple trip down memory lane floods your system with dopamine and serotonin, instantly lowering stress and helping you feel connected. Missing the past isn't a flaw; it's how your mind heals the present. What's one memory that instantly brings you comfort? Tell us in the comments!\n\n\ud83d\udd17 More facts + early access: tinyurl.com/238zsuaa\n\n#psychology #nostalgia #mentalhealth #brainfacts #learnontiktok"
